WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.243
This is strong-loop.

00:00:01.243 --> 00:00:04.412
Build the loop once, and run every role through it.

00:00:04.912 --> 00:00:12.183
Today, each analytics use case is its own agent project, with its own prompts, tools and guardrails.

00:00:12.183 --> 00:00:14.074
Ten use cases, ten builds.

00:00:14.074 --> 00:00:16.837
And none of them trusted to act alone.

00:00:17.337 --> 00:00:19.186
Here, the loop is built once.

00:00:19.186 --> 00:00:28.370
Each new use case is defined in a charter: what the role is responsible for, what it may do, what it must never touch, and what counts as proof.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:32.962
These four run on the same engine, with no code written for any of them.

00:00:33.462 --> 00:00:35.248
Autonomy has three parts.

00:00:35.248 --> 00:00:40.036
The model explores freely, round after round, with nobody watching.

00:00:40.036 --> 00:00:42.322
Fixed code decides what is true.

00:00:42.322 --> 00:00:53.112
And each action runs only at the level its charter grants: recommend, or act reversibly inside a cap, with a named person signing off where it matters.

00:00:53.612 --> 00:00:57.052
Before a run, it asks only what code cannot settle.

00:00:57.052 --> 00:01:02.987
Then the agent gets its brief: its goals, its permitted actions, and the proof it needs.

00:01:03.487 --> 00:01:07.902
Here is a real run: the claims analyst over 7,000 claims.

00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:11.001
Each round starts from an empty context.

00:01:11.001 --> 00:01:14.487
Its only memory is a ledger, written by code.

00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:17.914
It commits to each claim before seeing a result.

00:01:17.914 --> 00:01:22.549
Code tests it against the rows, and applies the charter's standard of proof.

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.386
A pass isn't enough.

00:01:24.386 --> 00:01:30.736
The same group is re-tested with a likely confound held constant, before a finding is recorded.

00:01:31.237 --> 00:01:37.687
An action needs a right the charter grants, evidence that clears its bar, and a size inside the cap.

00:01:38.187 --> 00:01:42.540
It stops when the ledger says so, not when the model says it's done.

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:47.150
Then every p-value is corrected together, and lucky results are demoted.

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:51.187
A new use case is a new charter, not a new agent.

00:01:51.187 --> 00:01:54.075
Write one for your own role, and run it.
